<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">4 events that happened on 29 September, from 1227 to 1938.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1227">1227 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">799 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Gregory IX excommunicates Emperor Frederick II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gregory IX excommunicated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> for again delaying his promised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>. Frederick went anyway, regaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> by treaty in 1229 and crowning himself in the Holy Sepulchre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1758">1758 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">268 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Horatio Nelson is born in Norfolk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> was born at Burnham Thorpe, the son of a rector. He won the battles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> and died at his greatest victory, Trafalgar, in 1805.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1829">1829 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">197 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">London's Metropolitan Police go on patrol for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Constables of Robert Peel's new Metropolitan Police began patrolling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. Nicknamed 'Bobbies' or 'Peelers', they set a model of uniformed, civilian policing by consent.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1938">1938 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Munich conference hands the Sudetenland to Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chamberlain, Daladier, Hitler and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> agreed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> must cede the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudetenland">Sudetenland</a>; the deal was signed after midnight. Czechoslovakia was not consulted.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a></div></div></li></ol>
